.TH GETGRENT_R 3
.SH NAME
getgrent_r, fgetgrent_r \- reentrant enumeration of the group database
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <grp.h>
.PP
.BI "int getgrent_r(struct group *" grbuf ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ,
.BI "struct group **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int fgetgrent_r(FILE *" stream ", struct group *" grbuf ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct group **" result ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the reentrant equivalents of
.BR getgrent (3)
and
.BR fgetgrent (3).
Each reads one group-database entry into the caller-supplied
.I grbuf
structure; its string fields and the
.I gr_mem
member-name vector are carved from the caller-supplied scratch buffer
.I buf
(length
.IR buflen ).
.I *result
is set to
.I grbuf
on success or NULL at end of file.
.TP
.B getgrent_r
returns the next entry from the internal stream positioned by
.BR setgrent (3)/ endgrent (3).
.TP
.B fgetgrent_r
reads the next entry from an already-open
.I stream
in
.IR /etc/group
format.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success.  At end of file
.B fgetgrent_r
returns ENOENT and
.I *result
is NULL.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I buf
was too small to hold the entry plus its member vector.
.TP
.B ENOENT
End of file (no more entries).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getgrent (3),
.BR getgrnam_r (3),
.BR getpwent_r (3),
.BR group (5)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX specifies
.BR getgrnam_r ;
.B getgrent_r
and
.B fgetgrent_r
are GNU extensions.
